IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-provisions`

-- Cross-references of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Victoria): one row for each place where one provision cites another provision of this Act, or a provision of another Act or instrument.
-- Generated by a script that reads the text file; a row carries the quoted words, the identifier cited, the section (or Part, Schedule, clause) of the index that holds it, and that heading as the index prints it.
-- A citation that names several provisions ("subsections (1), (2) and (2A)") gives one row for each provision named.
-- A paragraph range such as "paragraphs (e) to (f)" gives a row for every paragraph the text prints from the first to the last, in the order printed.

DECLARE VicCrossReferenceKind IS ONE OF
    VicReferenceWithinThisAct
    VicReferenceToAnotherInstrument

DECLARE VicCrossReference HAS
    `row`                                   IS A STRING
    `kind`                                  IS A VicCrossReferenceKind
    `citing provision`                      IS A STRING
    `words of the citation`                 IS A STRING
    `cited identifier`                      IS A STRING
    `cited provision in the index`          IS A STRING
    `heading of the cited provision`        IS A STRING
    `other instrument`                      IS A STRING
    `provision of the other instrument`     IS A STRING
    `line in the text`                      IS A NUMBER

-- src:66 | (1) The Acts passed in each calendar year shall be numbered in regular arithmetical series, beginning with the number 1, in the order in which they receive or, for the purposes of section 69 of the Constitution Act 1975, are deemed to have received the Royal Assent.
@ref xref 001 (src:66)
`xref 001` MEANS
    VicCrossReference OF "xref 001", VicReferenceToAnotherInstrument, "s 9(1)", "section 69 of the Constitution Act 1975", "", "", "", "Constitution Act 1975", "section 69", 66

-- src:76 | (3) A failure to comply with subsection (1) in a calendar year (whether the calendar year 2006 or any earlier or later calendar year) does not affect the validity, operation or effect of an Act passed in that year.
@ref xref 002 (src:76)
`xref 002` MEANS
    VicCrossReference OF "xref 002", VicReferenceWithinThisAct, "s 9(3)", "subsection (1)", "s 9(1)", "s 9", "Citation of Acts by number", "", "", 76

-- src:90 | (2AA) A citation of an Act by the title appearing before the enacting words or, if there is a preamble, before the preamble, being a citation that is in italics without bolding, is sufficient for the purposes of subsection (1).
@ref xref 003 (src:90)
`xref 003` MEANS
    VicCrossReference OF "xref 003", VicReferenceWithinThisAct, "s 10(2AA)", "subsection (1)", "s 10(1)", "s 10", "Citation of Acts by title", "", "", 90

-- src:94 | (2B) The alteration of a Bill to give effect to subsection (2A) is not to be taken to be an amendment of the Bill.
@ref xref 004 (src:94)
`xref 004` MEANS
    VicCrossReference OF "xref 004", VicReferenceWithinThisAct, "s 10(2B)", "subsection (2A)", "s 10(2A)", "s 10", "Citation of Acts by title", "", "", 94

-- src:110 | (1) Subject to subsection (2) and to section 71 of the Constitution Act 1975, if a particular day is fixed (whether in the Act or in a proclamation made under the Act) for an Act or a provision of an Act to come into operation, the Act or provision comes into operation at the beginning of that day.
@ref xref 005 (src:110)
`xref 005` MEANS
    VicCrossReference OF "xref 005", VicReferenceToAnotherInstrument, "s 11(1)", "section 71 of the Constitution Act 1975", "", "", "", "Constitution Act 1975", "section 71", 110

