-- The row is consistent with the index when: for a reference within this Act, the identifier cited is one the text prints, the section (or Part, Schedule or clause) that holds it is in the index,
-- and the heading on the row is the heading the index prints for it; for a reference to another instrument, the instrument is named.
GIVEN row IS A VicCrossReference
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`xref row is consistent with the index` MEANS
    CONSIDER row's `kind`
    WHEN VicReferenceToAnotherInstrument THEN NOT (row's `other instrument` EQUALS "")
    WHEN VicReferenceWithinThisAct THEN
        CONSIDER `entry of the provision index for an identifier` (row's `cited provision in the index`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST e THEN (`identifier is one the text prints` (row's `cited identifier`)) AND (e's `heading as printed` EQUALS row's `heading of the cited provision`)
